1
00:00:13,743 --> 00:00:16,037
If everyone's life had a genre,

2
00:00:16,538 --> 00:00:19,457
what would yours be?

3
00:00:24,129 --> 00:00:27,298
Film noir, with its murky underworld?

4
00:00:29,551 --> 00:00:32,887
A thriller driven by hidden crimes?

5
00:00:38,268 --> 00:00:41,146
Or a romantic comedy?

6
00:00:49,112 --> 00:00:50,446
What's the order, sir?

7
00:00:56,161 --> 00:00:59,330
Whatever the genre,
I'm sure everyone's lives are interesting.

8
00:01:01,541 --> 00:01:04,127
But why did mine have to be this one?

9
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:06,004
You have amnesia.

10
00:01:06,087 --> 00:01:09,465
You have a textbook case
of dissociative amnesia,

11
00:01:09,549 --> 00:01:12,468
meaning you've forgotten
key autobiographical details

12
00:01:12,552 --> 00:01:15,305
such as your name, age, or occupation.

13
00:01:15,388 --> 00:01:18,975
It's the same amnesia
you often see in dramas and movies.

14
00:01:19,058 --> 00:01:19,934
Exactly.

15
00:01:21,019 --> 00:01:22,395
-Sorry?
-This…

16
00:01:23,062 --> 00:01:24,522
It's actually possible?

17
00:01:26,191 --> 00:01:29,569
How can I not remember a single thing?

18
00:01:29,652 --> 00:01:31,863
It's not as common
as you see in dramas, but--

19
00:01:31,946 --> 00:01:33,615
And what normally happens in dramas?

20
00:01:35,158 --> 00:01:38,286
Well, they usually wake up,
turn to the person beside them,

21
00:01:38,369 --> 00:01:40,622
and ask with a vacant, innocent look,

22
00:01:40,705 --> 00:01:41,998
"Who are you?"

23
00:01:42,081 --> 00:01:43,208
Something like that.

24
00:01:43,791 --> 00:01:44,751
And where are they?

25
00:01:44,834 --> 00:01:48,630
The person I'm supposed to ask
"Who are you?" with an innocent look?

26
00:01:48,713 --> 00:01:51,382
Unfortunately, there is no one.

27
00:01:51,466 --> 00:01:52,508
No one?

28
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:57,013
You were unconscious
when you were brought in two weeks ago.

29
00:01:57,096 --> 00:01:59,515
You were found alone,
collapsed on the ground,

30
00:01:59,599 --> 00:02:01,517
and your body displayed
multiple signs of injury.

31
00:02:01,601 --> 00:02:04,812
And we couldn't use your fingerprints
to identify you, so…

32
00:02:09,525 --> 00:02:11,027
What the heck?

33
00:02:11,110 --> 00:02:13,988
When you were found,
your fingerprints were damaged.

34
00:02:14,072 --> 00:02:16,908
Without fingerprints,
we were unable to identify you,

35
00:02:16,991 --> 00:02:18,952
so we had no way
of contacting your family.

36
00:02:19,035 --> 00:02:22,413
Then shouldn't there have been
an investigation?

37
00:02:22,497 --> 00:02:24,958
The police tried to investigate
what happened,

38
00:02:25,041 --> 00:02:28,127
but you were found on a remote road
with no CCTV cameras.

39
00:02:28,211 --> 00:02:30,338
And they didn't find
any viable fingerprints

40
00:02:30,421 --> 00:02:33,967
on the clothes and shoes you were wearing
when you were found.

41
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:35,510
Okay, hold up.

42
00:02:35,593 --> 00:02:36,886
So, in a nutshell,

43
00:02:37,971 --> 00:02:41,140
I was found on the road and brought here
two weeks ago.

44
00:02:41,641 --> 00:02:45,061
You couldn't identify me.
The accident investigation was a bust.

45
00:02:45,144 --> 00:02:46,271
And I lost my memory?

46
00:02:47,814 --> 00:02:49,107
That's a perfect summary.

47
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:50,566
Then what should I do now?

48
00:02:50,650 --> 00:02:52,694
It would be great
if your memory returned--

49
00:02:52,777 --> 00:02:54,362
What if it doesn't?

50
00:02:54,445 --> 00:02:55,405
If it doesn't?

51
00:02:55,488 --> 00:02:57,615
You'll be classified as
an unidentified person,

52
00:02:57,699 --> 00:02:59,450
and once you've been treated,

53
00:02:59,534 --> 00:03:01,953
you'll be sent to a government facility.

54
00:03:06,582 --> 00:03:07,959
So, put simply,

55
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,878
I'm in a damn sticky mess.

56
00:03:10,962 --> 00:03:13,339
You really are excellent at summarizing.

57
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:15,967
That's a good sign.

58
00:03:25,393 --> 00:03:28,313
OUR STICKY LOVE

59
00:03:28,396 --> 00:03:30,231
Who are you?

60
00:03:30,315 --> 00:03:33,443
How did you end up here
after such a terrible accident?

61
00:03:34,944 --> 00:03:39,157
How is it possible that you don't even
remember your own name?

62
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,121
But…

63
00:03:46,873 --> 00:03:47,874
you're pretty.

64
00:03:52,045 --> 00:03:53,254
Check out this body.

65
00:03:54,756 --> 00:03:56,507
Abs? Why do you have abs?

66
00:03:56,591 --> 00:04:00,094
I must say, at first glance,
I really like what I see.

67
00:04:00,178 --> 00:04:03,348
With these looks,
you should have become a celebrity.

68
00:04:03,431 --> 00:04:04,932
Why didn't you?

69
00:04:05,016 --> 00:04:09,645
If you had, even if you had amnesia,
other people would have recognized you.

70
00:04:12,273 --> 00:04:14,233
Who the heck were you?

71
00:04:14,817 --> 00:04:18,446
Damn it, who the heck was I?

72
00:04:18,529 --> 00:04:21,032
Oh, come on!

73
00:04:27,121 --> 00:04:28,289
SANDEUL HOSPITAL

74
00:04:28,373 --> 00:04:30,208
ONE WEEK LATER

75
00:04:32,794 --> 00:04:34,003
Nowadays,

76
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:38,508
government-run facilities aren't half bad.

77
00:04:38,591 --> 00:04:39,425
That's right.

78
00:04:39,509 --> 00:04:41,803
I hear they even educate
North Korean refugees

79
00:04:41,886 --> 00:04:43,846
and help them find jobs.

80
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:46,891
Think of it as an opportunity
to start life anew.

81
00:04:46,974 --> 00:04:49,811
Go there and try to find
what you're good at.

82
00:04:49,894 --> 00:04:51,145
You scared me.

83
00:04:51,229 --> 00:04:53,356
Okay, let's try whatever.

84
00:04:53,439 --> 00:04:56,776
I lost my memory due to a head injury,
so if I stimulate it again,

85
00:04:56,859 --> 00:04:58,236
maybe it will come back.

86
00:04:58,319 --> 00:04:59,529
That's it. Attagirl.

87
00:05:01,656 --> 00:05:03,199
She's got her pep back.

88
00:05:03,282 --> 00:05:04,242
Fancy some peanuts?

89
00:05:09,455 --> 00:05:11,499
Good heavens!

90
00:05:11,582 --> 00:05:13,042
-Oh no!
-Goodness, dear.

91
00:05:13,126 --> 00:05:13,960
Oh my.

92
00:05:17,213 --> 00:05:18,756
Looks like she's coming to.

93
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,384
You should dial down the crazy.

94
00:05:21,467 --> 00:05:24,804
Why would you smash your noggin
into the wall like that?

95
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,682
Or you should've waited an hour to do it.

96
00:05:27,765 --> 00:05:28,599
Sorry?

97
00:05:28,683 --> 00:05:30,351
Shortly after you passed out,

98
00:05:30,435 --> 00:05:33,104
someone came by.

99
00:05:33,604 --> 00:05:35,189
Your boyfriend.

100
00:05:36,607 --> 00:05:38,693
Someone who actually knows you

101
00:05:38,776 --> 00:05:40,862
finally came for you!

102
00:05:41,362 --> 00:05:42,280
Really?

103
00:05:42,363 --> 00:05:45,992
Apparently, your boyfriend's been
looking for you like crazy.

104
00:05:47,034 --> 00:05:48,453
He has?

105
00:05:48,536 --> 00:05:49,662
And where is he?

106
00:05:49,745 --> 00:05:52,498
-My so-called boyfriend?
-Hold your horses. He'll be here soon.

107
00:05:53,708 --> 00:05:58,796
Your boyfriend's a strapping young man.
A total looker.

108
00:05:59,547 --> 00:06:01,424
I thought he was an actor.

109
00:06:03,801 --> 00:06:05,511
Aren't you lucky?

110
00:06:06,012 --> 00:06:07,221
He was totally my type.

111
00:06:07,305 --> 00:06:08,514
Thank God.

112
00:06:10,516 --> 00:06:11,809
Of course.

113
00:06:12,310 --> 00:06:15,188
Looking this good,
there's no way I'm single.

114
00:06:16,314 --> 00:06:19,317
I can finally find out who I am.

115
00:06:20,109 --> 00:06:23,362
You've been through so much, dear.

116
00:06:27,825 --> 00:06:29,785
I hear someone coming.

117
00:06:39,587 --> 00:06:40,421
Oh my…

118
00:06:44,425 --> 00:06:46,427
I hit the jackpot.

119
00:06:49,138 --> 00:06:50,139
Grandma.

120
00:06:51,807 --> 00:06:53,017
There you are.

121
00:06:54,143 --> 00:06:56,020
This is my grandson.

122
00:06:57,772 --> 00:06:59,357
He's a model.

123
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,442
-Say hello.
-Nice to meet you.

124
00:07:03,486 --> 00:07:05,613
I hear someone else coming.

125
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,968
You heard, didn't you?
That someone came for you.

126
00:07:28,594 --> 00:07:30,012
Shall we call him in?

127
00:07:32,098 --> 00:07:33,641
Come on in.

128
00:07:40,439 --> 00:07:43,317
HONG'S BOXING GYM

129
00:07:52,785 --> 00:07:53,619
Who the heck

130
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:57,248
is this scruffy, scrappy boxer?

131
00:08:04,589 --> 00:08:07,883
Why is Scrappy standing in front of me?

132
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,845
Go Eun-sae.

133
00:08:13,472 --> 00:08:16,350
You really don't remember anything?
You don't know who I am?

134
00:08:18,477 --> 00:08:20,146
Yes, I'd like to keep it that way.

135
00:08:23,733 --> 00:08:24,567
It's me.

136
00:08:25,693 --> 00:08:26,527
No.

137
00:08:27,528 --> 00:08:28,404
Jang Tae-ha.

138
00:08:28,487 --> 00:08:29,488
No.

139
00:08:30,781 --> 00:08:31,699
Please.

140
00:08:32,450 --> 00:08:33,492
Your boyfriend.

141
00:08:39,707 --> 00:08:40,833
Moving, isn't it?

142
00:08:41,667 --> 00:08:44,712
For three whole weeks,
he says he searched every hospital

143
00:08:45,212 --> 00:08:48,257
in Seoul, Gyeonggi,
and the entire capital area to find you.

144
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:52,428
I heard he was a looker…

145
00:08:52,928 --> 00:08:54,513
That he looked like an actor…

146
00:08:55,514 --> 00:08:57,642
His shoulders are as broad as a barn door.

147
00:08:57,725 --> 00:09:01,020
-Like a young Baek Il-seob.
-Looks like Park Geun-hyeong to me.

148
00:09:01,103 --> 00:09:04,106
That's exactly how Park looked
when he was young.

149
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,660
So, in a nutshell,

150
00:09:16,535 --> 00:09:18,120
my name is Go Eun-sae.

151
00:09:18,704 --> 00:09:19,538
As for age,

152
00:09:20,539 --> 00:09:21,415
I'm 33 years old.

153
00:09:21,499 --> 00:09:24,418
I work part-time at a taffy shop,
making taffy,

154
00:09:24,502 --> 00:09:27,838
and I've been dating you,
a boxing coach, for two years,

155
00:09:27,922 --> 00:09:31,258
and we live together,
even looking to get married soon?

156
00:09:44,814 --> 00:09:47,233
Well, what to do?
I don't believe any of that.

157
00:09:47,316 --> 00:09:50,778
For starters, how could I not have
a proper job at 33?

158
00:09:50,861 --> 00:09:53,489
You were an aspiring web novel writer
who never made it.

159
00:09:53,572 --> 00:09:56,909
So you started working at
my grandmother's taffy shop a month ago.

160
00:09:57,535 --> 00:10:00,788
Then do you have any proof
that we're dating?

161
00:10:11,882 --> 00:10:13,050
Hey, come on.

162
00:10:13,134 --> 00:10:16,637
This couldn't possibly be proof
that we're dating.

163
00:10:16,721 --> 00:10:20,182
This could be two tourists passing by
who happened to be snapped together.

164
00:10:22,184 --> 00:10:23,018
Any other photos?

165
00:10:23,602 --> 00:10:26,230
-This is the only one.
-See?

166
00:10:26,313 --> 00:10:28,816
How is that possible
when we dated for two years?

167
00:10:28,899 --> 00:10:33,279
I lost my phone while running around
looking for you these past three weeks.

168
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:36,824
-It had all our photos.
-You expect me to believe that?

169
00:10:36,907 --> 00:10:39,034
It would've helped
if we had your phone,

170
00:10:39,618 --> 00:10:41,912
but, as you know,
they found you with nothing.

171
00:10:41,996 --> 00:10:46,417
I have no clue what happened to you
after you went out to meet a friend,

172
00:10:47,168 --> 00:10:48,335
but for now,

173
00:10:50,129 --> 00:10:51,422
I'm just glad you're alive.

174
00:10:56,093 --> 00:10:57,303
Do you

175
00:10:57,803 --> 00:11:00,181
usually not wash up?

176
00:11:06,729 --> 00:11:07,688
Oh, I…

177
00:11:07,772 --> 00:11:13,110
Well, my car broke down on the way here,
so I had to fix it in a hurry.

178
00:11:13,194 --> 00:11:14,612
And you don't shave?

179
00:11:14,695 --> 00:11:15,738
Shave?

180
00:11:16,238 --> 00:11:18,949
It's been a bit hectic recently.

181
00:11:22,661 --> 00:11:23,829
Fine, I get it.

182
00:11:23,913 --> 00:11:27,291
Can you just reach out
to my family for me?

183
00:11:28,375 --> 00:11:29,502
You don't have any.

184
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:31,754
I don't have any?

185
00:11:31,837 --> 00:11:34,006
You grew up in an orphanage.

186
00:11:39,595 --> 00:11:41,305
Hold on.

187
00:11:41,388 --> 00:11:43,974
So I don't have any family,

188
00:11:44,475 --> 00:11:47,144
I lost my phone,
so I don't have any friends' numbers,

189
00:11:47,228 --> 00:11:51,357
and I'm an aspiring web novel writer,
so I don't have any colleagues.

190
00:11:52,066 --> 00:11:53,984
So, in other words,

191
00:11:54,068 --> 00:11:56,320
you're the only one I have
in the whole world?

192
00:11:56,904 --> 00:11:57,947
Is that right?

193
00:11:59,198 --> 00:12:01,784
As I said,
you're excellent at summarizing.

194
00:12:07,873 --> 00:12:10,626
If you're done talking, you can go home.

195
00:12:10,709 --> 00:12:13,963
You can get the rest of your treatment
as an outpatient.

196
00:12:15,965 --> 00:12:18,175
Can I talk to you for a second?

197
00:12:18,676 --> 00:12:19,760
Sure, yes.

198
00:12:22,721 --> 00:12:25,391
You should go wash your face or something.

199
00:12:30,688 --> 00:12:34,400
How can you just believe he's my boyfriend
and let him take me home?

200
00:12:34,483 --> 00:12:36,861
We checked with the police,

201
00:12:36,944 --> 00:12:41,073
and the person he's been looking for
matched your description perfectly.

202
00:12:42,199 --> 00:12:44,869
He even knew about
the triangle of moles on your butt.

203
00:12:44,952 --> 00:12:46,912
He got it exactly right.

204
00:12:46,996 --> 00:12:48,247
Moles on my butt?

205
00:12:48,330 --> 00:12:51,250
Yes, we all saw them
when we were treating you.

206
00:12:51,333 --> 00:12:55,963
Just here on your right butt cheek,
you have a triangle of moles.

207
00:12:56,046 --> 00:12:59,758
And the mole at the very top
is a little different in color.

208
00:12:59,842 --> 00:13:01,427
Greenish, if you will.

209
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:04,096
He even got that right.

210
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:09,727
Quite frankly,
those sorts of details are things

211
00:13:09,810 --> 00:13:11,562
only a boyfriend would know.

212
00:13:12,646 --> 00:13:14,607
Even so, how could you let me go

213
00:13:14,690 --> 00:13:16,775
with a complete stranger--

214
00:13:16,859 --> 00:13:19,361
If you don't believe him,
you can refuse to go with him.

215
00:13:20,321 --> 00:13:22,323
You can wait here for the police

216
00:13:22,406 --> 00:13:25,409
to escort you to a government facility.

217
00:13:32,875 --> 00:13:35,836
It's true. They're in a triangle,
and one's a different color.

218
00:13:37,421 --> 00:13:38,422
So,

219
00:13:38,505 --> 00:13:41,008
everything that guy said is true?

220
00:13:47,097 --> 00:13:49,433
Okay, I'll go with him for now.

221
00:13:49,934 --> 00:13:53,103
Who knows? Maybe going back
to where I lived will jog my memory.

222
00:13:59,735 --> 00:14:01,320
I used to wear this?

223
00:14:01,904 --> 00:14:03,530
I really wore something so tacky?

224
00:14:14,124 --> 00:14:16,085
You have to take these three times a week…

225
00:14:16,168 --> 00:14:18,295
I mean, three times a day.

226
00:14:23,342 --> 00:14:24,176
So what now?

227
00:14:25,427 --> 00:14:26,553
Do we go home?

228
00:14:27,763 --> 00:14:28,597
Yeah.

229
00:14:38,190 --> 00:14:39,525
Wait.

230
00:14:40,109 --> 00:14:41,735
Why are we going there, not Seoul?

231
00:14:41,819 --> 00:14:42,903
We don't live in Seoul.

232
00:14:44,029 --> 00:14:45,656
Don't be ridiculous.

233
00:14:45,739 --> 00:14:47,491
I may not remember who I am,

234
00:14:47,574 --> 00:14:50,536
but I remember
the Seoul subway map up to Line 9.

235
00:14:50,619 --> 00:14:54,039
We used to live in Seoul,
but we moved to Gujin two months ago.

236
00:14:54,123 --> 00:14:55,749
We… What?

237
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:57,626
Where the heck is Gujin?

238
00:14:58,335 --> 00:14:59,294
My hometown.

239
00:15:13,517 --> 00:15:15,602
HONG'S BOXING GYM

240
00:15:26,155 --> 00:15:29,033
GUJIN TAFFY VILLAGE

241
00:15:39,793 --> 00:15:41,879
GUJIN TAFFY VILLAGE

242
00:15:47,426 --> 00:15:49,094
The rice came out perfect!

243
00:15:50,971 --> 00:15:52,347
Come on, you can do better.

244
00:15:52,973 --> 00:15:54,975
-Isn't the rice good?
-Tae-ha, you're back?

245
00:15:55,559 --> 00:15:56,477
Yes, ma'am.

246
00:15:57,770 --> 00:15:59,646
Careful, now.

247
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:20,834
GUJIN-GUN TRADITIONAL RICE TAFFY

248
00:16:46,985 --> 00:16:47,820
Hello.

249
00:16:48,487 --> 00:16:50,322
-Hey.
-Hi!

250
00:16:51,323 --> 00:16:52,533
-Must be her.
-That her?

251
00:16:56,078 --> 00:16:56,954
What the…

252
00:16:57,704 --> 00:16:59,206
Who are those rough-looking women?

253
00:17:02,918 --> 00:17:06,130
If I knew I'd be lucky enough
to see your face today,

254
00:17:06,213 --> 00:17:08,507
I would've worn my glasses.

255
00:17:09,007 --> 00:17:10,342
This is her, isn't it?

256
00:17:10,425 --> 00:17:12,803
Your future missus
who came from Seoul with you?

257
00:17:12,886 --> 00:17:14,054
Yes.

258
00:17:15,305 --> 00:17:17,349
Say hello. They're from this village.

259
00:17:20,894 --> 00:17:21,895
Do you know me?

260
00:17:21,979 --> 00:17:24,189
Why, are you famous or something?

261
00:17:24,273 --> 00:17:26,108
-How would we know you?
-You don't?

262
00:17:26,191 --> 00:17:28,152
Never seen me around?
Apparently I live here.

263
00:17:28,235 --> 00:17:30,737
Well, that's the thing, isn't it?

264
00:17:30,821 --> 00:17:34,449
You came here almost two months ago,
but it's the first time you've graced us.

265
00:17:34,533 --> 00:17:36,827
So how could we have seen you?

266
00:17:38,078 --> 00:17:41,415
I apologize. We've had a lot going on.

267
00:17:41,498 --> 00:17:43,500
I'll tell you the details later.

268
00:17:43,584 --> 00:17:45,043
-Sure.
-You do that.

269
00:17:45,919 --> 00:17:47,296
You can get going now.

270
00:17:47,379 --> 00:17:49,006
You're in my way.

271
00:17:54,761 --> 00:17:56,263
I'll get going…

272
00:17:58,557 --> 00:17:59,641
so move out of my way.

273
00:18:09,026 --> 00:18:09,860
Tae-ha,

274
00:18:11,195 --> 00:18:12,029
what's with her?

275
00:18:17,034 --> 00:18:18,076
Tae-ha.

276
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,411
She's…

277
00:18:19,912 --> 00:18:20,954
Oh boy, Tae-ha.

278
00:18:24,958 --> 00:18:28,837
Wow, what a character.

279
00:18:28,921 --> 00:18:30,839
That one's no ordinary girl, is she?

280
00:18:30,923 --> 00:18:31,757
Definitely not.

281
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:35,552
She's clearly one of those rude Gen Z kids
who left their manners behind.

282
00:18:36,136 --> 00:18:39,598
She and I will never get along,
not in a million years.

283
00:18:54,154 --> 00:18:55,489
-Hello, I'm--
-Song-wol.

284
00:18:55,572 --> 00:18:58,617
I told you, right?
She doesn't remember anything.

285
00:19:01,203 --> 00:19:04,164
Do you know me? Did I really work here?

286
00:19:07,876 --> 00:19:09,962
And what about him?
Is he really my boyfriend?

287
00:19:16,802 --> 00:19:19,471
Please tell me everything
you know about me.

288
00:19:21,014 --> 00:19:25,143
Come on, just tell me.
You don't have to worry about him.

289
00:19:26,478 --> 00:19:28,605
She can't speak. She has aphasia.

290
00:19:30,482 --> 00:19:33,193
Her name is Kim Song-wol,
and she's from North Korea.

291
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:37,781
She can't speak,
but she can hear and read just fine,

292
00:19:37,864 --> 00:19:40,367
so communication isn't a problem.

293
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:48,667
Excuse me, ma'am.

294
00:19:49,167 --> 00:19:50,585
Ma'am, did I really--

295
00:19:50,669 --> 00:19:54,131
Keep it down, old lady!
Go outside and choke on some taffy.

296
00:19:57,009 --> 00:19:58,844
What did you just say?

297
00:19:58,927 --> 00:20:00,429
My grandma has dementia.

298
00:20:00,512 --> 00:20:02,180
She didn't mean to be rude--

299
00:20:02,264 --> 00:20:03,140
No, not that.

300
00:20:03,223 --> 00:20:04,558
"Old lady"?

301
00:20:04,641 --> 00:20:07,769
Why would you call me an old lady?

302
00:20:07,853 --> 00:20:09,730
Why would you call me old?

303
00:20:09,813 --> 00:20:13,483
If you're going to be that darn loud,
you should've become a singer.

304
00:20:13,567 --> 00:20:15,444
Goodness, you're hurting my ears.

305
00:20:15,944 --> 00:20:17,946
Honey, take this old lady outside.

306
00:20:24,995 --> 00:20:26,955
What a crazy bitch.

307
00:20:30,459 --> 00:20:32,669
One has dementia,
and the other has aphasia.

308
00:20:34,212 --> 00:20:35,881
There's really no one I can ask?

309
00:20:35,964 --> 00:20:38,300
Let's go home now.
You should get some rest.

310
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:43,263
By "home," you mean the house
we used to live in, right?

311
00:20:59,446 --> 00:21:00,655
This is our home.

312
00:21:06,870 --> 00:21:07,704
Well…

313
00:21:13,543 --> 00:21:14,378
Hold up.

314
00:21:16,088 --> 00:21:16,922
Wait a minute.

315
00:21:17,422 --> 00:21:19,424
Why's it barking at me?

316
00:21:20,592 --> 00:21:23,970
If I used to live here,
it should run over, wagging its tail.

317
00:21:24,054 --> 00:21:27,265
Why is it barking at me
like I'm a complete stranger?

318
00:21:28,975 --> 00:21:29,851
It's not our dog.

319
00:21:32,896 --> 00:21:33,814
It was in there.

320
00:21:34,856 --> 00:21:35,941
That's village dogs for you.

321
00:21:36,024 --> 00:21:37,901
They wander around

322
00:21:37,984 --> 00:21:40,821
and eat and sleep
if they find a doghouse they fancy.

323
00:21:41,363 --> 00:21:43,490
It's been staying here the past few days.

324
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,034
Are you serious?

325
00:21:46,118 --> 00:21:49,413
Thankfully, it doesn't bark for long.
It stops after a few barks.

326
00:21:52,374 --> 00:21:53,333
This is killing me.

327
00:21:54,918 --> 00:21:56,002
That makes no sense.

328
00:22:19,985 --> 00:22:23,530
Flowers, flowers, flowers, and flowers.
Flowers everywhere.

329
00:22:24,573 --> 00:22:27,784
Has this blanket been in the family
for three generations or something?

330
00:22:27,868 --> 00:22:30,829
-It was bought recently--
-No way someone paid money for this.

331
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:34,749
What's with this bed?

332
00:22:42,215 --> 00:22:43,925
How very old-school soap opera.

333
00:22:49,014 --> 00:22:50,307
Is this chicken soup?

334
00:22:50,390 --> 00:22:52,726
Why is there reishi mushroom in lotion?

335
00:22:53,894 --> 00:22:56,104
This was really expensive…

336
00:23:00,609 --> 00:23:01,776
I'm sure of it.

337
00:23:02,527 --> 00:23:03,445
I didn't live here.

338
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,405
Why do you think that?

339
00:23:05,489 --> 00:23:09,493
Because I don't like a single thing
in this house.

340
00:23:10,494 --> 00:23:11,870
You hated superficial things,

341
00:23:11,953 --> 00:23:13,830
so we didn't renovate when we moved in--

342
00:23:13,914 --> 00:23:17,375
I'm the girl who cropped my hospital gown.

343
00:23:17,459 --> 00:23:20,670
You're saying I hated superficial things
when I loved to get dolled up?

344
00:23:22,422 --> 00:23:25,467
And how come there's none of your stuff
in the bedroom?

345
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:28,678
If we were due to get married,
we must have shared a room.

346
00:23:30,430 --> 00:23:32,265
When I found out the state you were in,

347
00:23:32,349 --> 00:23:34,518
I moved all of my stuff there.

348
00:23:34,601 --> 00:23:37,187
For you, it'd be like
sleeping with a man you just met.

349
00:23:37,270 --> 00:23:38,647
It would be strange.

350
00:23:39,856 --> 00:23:42,150
-So you were being considerate?
-Yes.

351
00:23:47,364 --> 00:23:48,823
Your name's Jang Tae-ha, right?

352
00:23:50,534 --> 00:23:51,368
Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

353
00:23:51,451 --> 00:23:54,246
Tell me about how we met.

354
00:23:54,329 --> 00:23:57,582
I'm finding it hard to believe
any of this, so start from the beginning.

355
00:23:57,666 --> 00:24:00,418
A blind date?
Or did you make the first move?

356
00:24:00,502 --> 00:24:06,132
I need to know how and why
I ended up living with you.

357
00:24:14,474 --> 00:24:16,059
We met in the mountains.

358
00:24:19,604 --> 00:24:21,189
What are you looking at?

359
00:24:58,977 --> 00:25:01,396
You can continue on your way. I've got it.

360
00:25:14,784 --> 00:25:16,911
Are you freaking kidding me?

361
00:25:16,995 --> 00:25:19,581
I fell for you
just because you caught a toad?

362
00:25:19,664 --> 00:25:22,250
You just wouldn't stop chasing me.

363
00:25:22,334 --> 00:25:24,586
Whoa, wait. What did you say?

364
00:25:24,669 --> 00:25:26,755
I pursued you? Not the other way around?

365
00:25:27,255 --> 00:25:30,091
You said you'd kill yourself
if I didn't go out with you, so I did.

366
00:25:30,175 --> 00:25:33,345
One day, you showed up with your stuff,
so we started living together.

367
00:25:33,428 --> 00:25:37,349
You insisted you couldn't live without me,
so we decided to get married.

368
00:25:37,432 --> 00:25:39,476
Wait. Hold it right there.

369
00:25:40,268 --> 00:25:41,645
Look, Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

370
00:25:41,728 --> 00:25:45,607
Just because I don't remember anything
doesn't mean you can just make things up.

371
00:25:45,690 --> 00:25:48,735
I haven't believed
anything you've said so far,

372
00:25:48,818 --> 00:25:50,945
and this is by far the most unbelievable.

373
00:25:51,029 --> 00:25:52,072
Should I go on?

374
00:25:52,155 --> 00:25:54,949
No, thank you.
Are you trying to give me a heart attack?

375
00:25:55,909 --> 00:25:59,245
Then get some rest. I'll be right back
after returning the car to the gym.

376
00:26:17,180 --> 00:26:19,683
HONG'S BOXING GYM

377
00:26:19,766 --> 00:26:21,685
All right, good!

378
00:26:21,768 --> 00:26:22,602
One more time.

379
00:26:24,270 --> 00:26:26,940
One-two! Again.

380
00:26:27,023 --> 00:26:28,400
Again, one-two!

381
00:26:28,483 --> 00:26:29,317
Good!

382
00:26:30,026 --> 00:26:31,236
What's wrong?

383
00:26:32,570 --> 00:26:33,863
Your shirt's still half dry.

384
00:26:34,447 --> 00:26:35,281
Get up.

385
00:26:35,865 --> 00:26:36,741
On your feet!

386
00:26:41,788 --> 00:26:42,706
Enough for today.

387
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:44,916
Thank you, sir.

388
00:26:44,999 --> 00:26:47,085
The more you sweat during training,

389
00:26:47,168 --> 00:26:49,129
the less you bleed during a match.

390
00:26:49,212 --> 00:26:51,631
I'll sweat buckets tomorrow.

391
00:26:52,507 --> 00:26:53,508
If you say so.

392
00:26:57,303 --> 00:26:58,304
There you are.

393
00:26:58,388 --> 00:26:59,264
Yes, sir.

394
00:27:00,473 --> 00:27:01,766
Hello, Coach.

395
00:27:01,850 --> 00:27:02,809
Good work, Pil-seung.

396
00:27:04,853 --> 00:27:06,688
-Sir, I'll be going now.
-Okay.

397
00:27:06,771 --> 00:27:08,440
-Go on.
-Okay. Goodbye.

398
00:27:08,523 --> 00:27:10,316
-Hey, run all the way home.
-Yes, sir!

399
00:27:17,031 --> 00:27:19,159
Hey, how did it go?

400
00:27:19,242 --> 00:27:20,410
Did you bring her back okay?

401
00:27:23,371 --> 00:27:25,457
She doesn't seem to believe me.

402
00:27:26,499 --> 00:27:27,375
Figures.

403
00:27:27,459 --> 00:27:30,378
She must be used to
living in luxury in Seoul.

404
00:27:30,462 --> 00:27:33,840
Something inside her
must be resisting the countryside.

405
00:27:34,799 --> 00:27:35,633
Do you think

406
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:37,761
it'll be okay?

407
00:27:40,096 --> 00:27:42,640
We can't get caught, no matter what.

408
00:27:46,102 --> 00:27:48,480
3 WEEKS AGO

409
00:28:07,957 --> 00:28:11,169
This is a reserved space,
so you can't park here. Please move.

410
00:28:12,378 --> 00:28:13,922
-You must be new here.
-Sorry?

411
00:28:14,672 --> 00:28:16,800
Yes. You must frequent
the Prosecutors' Office

412
00:28:16,883 --> 00:28:18,802
to notice a change in security detail.

413
00:28:19,385 --> 00:28:21,471
I have, for about three years now.

414
00:28:22,055 --> 00:28:25,058
I changed my car over the weekend,
so it's not registered yet.

415
00:28:25,642 --> 00:28:27,852
-But this is my parking space.
-Sorry?

416
00:28:28,978 --> 00:28:32,315
And I'll continue to frequent this place,
so please remember my face.

417
00:28:35,026 --> 00:28:39,072
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Anti-Corruption Department.

418
00:28:42,742 --> 00:28:46,329
And this here is our top gun,
Prosecutor Go Ji-won.

419
00:28:46,412 --> 00:28:48,373
You saw her at the inauguration, right?

420
00:28:48,456 --> 00:28:52,293
Yes. How could I forget someone
with such a unique presence?

421
00:28:55,088 --> 00:28:57,423
I have many other
exceptional qualities, Chief.

422
00:28:59,008 --> 00:29:01,594
You'll see them soon in my work.

423
00:29:11,020 --> 00:29:12,021
If you'll excuse me…

424
00:29:12,522 --> 00:29:15,149
Mr. Mayor, this is my girlfriend.

425
00:29:16,359 --> 00:29:19,028
Hello, I'm Go Ji-won
from the Prosecutors' Office.

426
00:29:19,112 --> 00:29:22,448
Yes, I've heard a lot about you.
An anti-corruption prosecutor, correct?

427
00:29:22,532 --> 00:29:25,535
Anti-corruption?
You must be one of the elite.

428
00:29:26,619 --> 00:29:30,081
This is Chairman Baek Sang-gil
of Mirae Eden Company.

429
00:29:30,957 --> 00:29:31,791
I'm well aware.

430
00:29:35,503 --> 00:29:37,755
I found your guest introduction
rather memorable.

431
00:29:42,302 --> 00:29:43,511
It's nice to meet you.

432
00:29:47,807 --> 00:29:49,642
I'll leave you to it, then.

433
00:29:50,643 --> 00:29:52,103
-I'll be right back.
-Okay.

434
00:29:56,316 --> 00:30:00,445
The mayor and Chairman Baek will leave
the venue between 10:00 and 10:10.

435
00:30:00,528 --> 00:30:02,405
I'm only escorting the mayor to the venue.

436
00:30:02,488 --> 00:30:06,159
The official plan is that
the mayor's driver will take him home.

437
00:30:06,659 --> 00:30:09,996
But instead of going home,
he'll be making contact?

438
00:30:11,205 --> 00:30:12,081
Don't worry.

439
00:30:12,665 --> 00:30:15,418
This is valuable intel
my aide boyfriend managed to get me.

440
00:30:17,086 --> 00:30:18,087
I have to make this work.

441
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:11,099
You'll have to wait a bit longer
for the final decision on the contractor

442
00:31:11,599 --> 00:31:13,059
for the Irang-dong project.

443
00:31:13,559 --> 00:31:18,189
There are a lot of eyes on this,
so it's hard to speed things up.

444
00:31:21,985 --> 00:31:25,446
Before we bring the thunder,

445
00:31:25,530 --> 00:31:28,241
it'd be best for you
to take care of it swiftly.

446
00:31:29,575 --> 00:31:32,286
We wouldn't want the thunder
to be followed by a downpour,

447
00:31:33,913 --> 00:31:35,415
leaving our dear mayor's

448
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,085
royal robes be drenched, would we now?

449
00:32:24,047 --> 00:32:27,717
You'll have to wait a bit longer
for the final decision on the contractor

450
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:29,093
for the Irang-dong project.

451
00:32:31,763 --> 00:32:33,389
We meet again, Prosecutor.

452
00:32:44,233 --> 00:32:45,068
Looks like it.

453
00:32:46,277 --> 00:32:48,196
Though not in the most dignified place.

454
00:32:52,575 --> 00:32:56,412
We only got word of your visit
at the last second,

455
00:32:57,997 --> 00:33:00,374
so we ended up showing you
an unseemly side.

456
00:33:01,334 --> 00:33:04,337
Given the chance to make it up to you,
we'd treat you handsomely.

457
00:33:06,672 --> 00:33:07,590
As for your watch…

458
00:33:09,717 --> 00:33:11,761
we'd replace it quite generously.

459
00:33:20,228 --> 00:33:23,856
I guess you think
prosecutors in Korea are a joke.

460
00:33:25,733 --> 00:33:27,235
I'm loaded.

461
00:33:27,735 --> 00:33:30,029
I don't need your dirty money to get by.

462
00:33:36,285 --> 00:33:38,287
If you're waiting for your investigators,

463
00:33:39,038 --> 00:33:42,625
my men have gone to greet them,
so no need to worry too much.

464
00:33:45,294 --> 00:33:47,463
So, Prosecutor,

465
00:33:48,548 --> 00:33:50,007
what will you do now?

466
00:33:55,179 --> 00:33:56,764
Crazy bastard.

467
00:34:23,082 --> 00:34:24,083
Seriously?

468
00:34:25,835 --> 00:34:27,503
You bastards want to…

469
00:34:28,921 --> 00:34:29,755
Hey!

470
00:34:33,593 --> 00:34:34,552
What the…

471
00:35:05,208 --> 00:35:07,460
You know,
I don't really watch movies anymore.

472
00:35:08,586 --> 00:35:10,546
The ending's already decided,

473
00:35:10,630 --> 00:35:13,799
and wasting all that time
just to watch it unfold…

474
00:35:16,802 --> 00:35:18,304
seems fucking stupid.

475
00:35:43,246 --> 00:35:44,705
I'm saying, don't even bother.

476
00:36:04,517 --> 00:36:06,018
Hey! Get over here, damn it!

477
00:36:09,772 --> 00:36:10,898
Fuck!

478
00:36:40,011 --> 00:36:43,639
You'll have to wait a bit longer
for the final decision on the contractor

479
00:36:43,723 --> 00:36:45,141
for the Irang-dong project.

480
00:36:45,224 --> 00:36:47,018
There are a lot of eyes on this,

481
00:36:47,601 --> 00:36:49,937
so it's hard to speed things up.

482
00:36:52,231 --> 00:36:54,233
What should we do now?

483
00:37:02,283 --> 00:37:04,994
NARITA, TOKYO
LANDED

484
00:38:03,260 --> 00:38:04,345
I got the sales report.

485
00:38:05,179 --> 00:38:06,680
Thanks to you, Director Jang,

486
00:38:06,764 --> 00:38:08,682
the Tokyo pachinko business
is faring well.

487
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:10,434
Not at all.

488
00:38:13,687 --> 00:38:14,563
Tae-ha.

489
00:38:15,481 --> 00:38:16,315
Yes, sir?

490
00:38:17,858 --> 00:38:18,776
You told me recently

491
00:38:19,443 --> 00:38:21,904
that you wanted
to leave this world behind.

492
00:38:31,914 --> 00:38:32,748
You may leave.

493
00:38:35,501 --> 00:38:36,502
Sir?

494
00:38:41,674 --> 00:38:45,970
You're the one who turned Geukrakpa,
some back-alley gang, into Mirae Eden.

495
00:38:46,053 --> 00:38:47,847
You deserve that much.

496
00:38:52,393 --> 00:38:53,227
Sir.

497
00:38:58,858 --> 00:39:01,819
Just do one last job for me
before you leave.

498
00:39:03,362 --> 00:39:05,114
We need to take care of a prosecutor.

499
00:39:05,823 --> 00:39:08,784
It is a prosecutor we're talking about,
so things could get messy.

500
00:39:16,333 --> 00:39:18,335
I need someone I can trust.

501
00:39:20,421 --> 00:39:23,549
Think of it as giving me a parting gift.

502
00:39:24,592 --> 00:39:25,468
Tae-ha.

503
00:39:26,844 --> 00:39:28,095
Can you do it for me?

504
00:39:45,696 --> 00:39:46,697
Current condition?

505
00:39:47,823 --> 00:39:48,782
Almost out.

506
00:40:27,905 --> 00:40:29,156
What's the order, sir?

507
00:40:38,415 --> 00:40:40,376
-Forget it.
-Sorry?

508
00:40:46,006 --> 00:40:48,592
Chairman Baek asked me
to take care of this myself.

509
00:40:50,553 --> 00:40:52,012
Don't get your hands dirty.

510
00:40:53,806 --> 00:40:55,015
I'll do it myself.

511
00:41:06,735 --> 00:41:08,153
HONG DO-YEOP

512
00:41:13,200 --> 00:41:14,285
I need your help.

513
00:41:14,868 --> 00:41:16,412
I have to save someone.

514
00:41:23,836 --> 00:41:27,339
I'm certain Baek Sang-gil will scrutinize
every step of the process,

515
00:41:27,923 --> 00:41:30,801
illegally securing traffic CCTV footage
if necessary.

516
00:41:30,884 --> 00:41:34,888
Fortunately, there is exactly one place
on the way to the final destination

517
00:41:34,972 --> 00:41:36,307
that's a CCTV blind spot.

518
00:42:25,397 --> 00:42:26,231
Okay.

519
00:43:20,369 --> 00:43:22,454
I assume you didn't leave any crumbs.

520
00:43:23,914 --> 00:43:24,748
Yes, sir.

521
00:43:29,586 --> 00:43:30,629
Good work.

522
00:43:39,054 --> 00:43:41,724
SANDEUL HOSPITAL

523
00:43:43,225 --> 00:43:45,185
How could this happen?

524
00:43:45,269 --> 00:43:47,813
She finally woke up after two weeks…

525
00:43:52,025 --> 00:43:52,985
UNKNOWN, F, 20S

526
00:43:53,068 --> 00:43:54,611
…but she has amnesia.

527
00:44:00,617 --> 00:44:02,453
Since she has no fingerprints,

528
00:44:02,536 --> 00:44:06,248
she'll be listed as unidentified
and placed in a government facility.

529
00:44:07,666 --> 00:44:09,084
Wouldn't that be too risky?

530
00:44:09,168 --> 00:44:11,086
She must be kept from the outside world.

531
00:44:12,045 --> 00:44:16,508
In this situation,
it'd be safest to keep her by your side.

532
00:44:16,592 --> 00:44:20,137
But to do that, you would need to have
a valid reason to take her home.

533
00:44:20,220 --> 00:44:22,473
If you were family, for example.

534
00:44:22,556 --> 00:44:24,266
Or someone who is to become family,

535
00:44:25,476 --> 00:44:26,894
like a fiancé.

536
00:44:37,863 --> 00:44:41,658
The doctor said it's probably
a temporary aftereffect of the accident.

537
00:44:41,742 --> 00:44:45,245
Surely her memory will come back
once she recovers.

538
00:44:47,956 --> 00:44:49,333
By the way,

539
00:44:51,001 --> 00:44:53,045
have you found a stowaway boat for Japan?

540
00:44:53,670 --> 00:44:55,547
Kaito is looking for local brokers.

541
00:44:57,216 --> 00:44:58,091
Okay, good.

542
00:44:58,175 --> 00:45:01,804
Once her memory comes back
and the boat's ready, we'll send her off.

543
00:45:01,887 --> 00:45:03,222
Then it'll all be over.

544
00:45:03,722 --> 00:45:06,683
Until then, we have to keep her here.

545
00:45:06,767 --> 00:45:10,020
So just bite the bullet.
Pretend to be her boyfriend for a while.

546
00:45:13,482 --> 00:45:14,316
Okay.

547
00:45:18,278 --> 00:45:20,155
Hey, don't worry too much.

548
00:45:20,239 --> 00:45:21,657
We're in the middle of nowhere,

549
00:45:21,740 --> 00:45:24,660
the kind of backwater
where nothing's changed in years.

550
00:45:24,743 --> 00:45:27,412
There's no place safer than this.

551
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:33,544
No matter how I look at it,

552
00:45:34,878 --> 00:45:35,963
it's too unfamiliar.

553
00:45:36,046 --> 00:45:39,383
Just because I lost my memory,
it doesn't mean I lost my intuition.

554
00:45:39,466 --> 00:45:44,680
How can every corner of the house,
every last spoon, feel so unfamiliar?

555
00:45:48,100 --> 00:45:49,852
Come on.

556
00:45:49,935 --> 00:45:52,437
If only these were fine.

557
00:45:52,521 --> 00:45:55,524
I wouldn't be this frustrated. Seriously.

558
00:45:59,319 --> 00:46:01,613
Just what kind of accident did I get into?

559
00:46:15,252 --> 00:46:18,171
What's that? Is that…

560
00:46:41,904 --> 00:46:43,030
What are you doing?

561
00:46:58,837 --> 00:46:59,922
Did you get

562
00:47:00,797 --> 00:47:02,174
your memory back?

563
00:47:02,758 --> 00:47:03,634
Why?

564
00:47:03,717 --> 00:47:05,177
Are you scared I might

565
00:47:05,761 --> 00:47:06,720
get it back?

566
00:47:10,265 --> 00:47:12,601
Unfortunately, my memory hasn't come back,

567
00:47:13,185 --> 00:47:14,770
but I did see something.

568
00:47:20,776 --> 00:47:22,361
I found this in the yard.

569
00:47:22,444 --> 00:47:25,197
You said I fell for you
because you caught one for me,

570
00:47:25,280 --> 00:47:27,199
but I'm not scared of it at all.

571
00:47:28,200 --> 00:47:29,701
I could even keep it as a pet.

572
00:47:29,785 --> 00:47:31,078
Hey, can you…

573
00:47:38,835 --> 00:47:39,670
What's going on?

574
00:47:43,882 --> 00:47:45,842
I guess you lost your fear
with your memory.

575
00:47:45,926 --> 00:47:47,302
Don't be ridiculous.

576
00:47:50,973 --> 00:47:54,226
The doctor said head injuries
can cause all sorts of aftereffects.

577
00:47:54,309 --> 00:47:56,228
You're not my boyfriend, are you?

578
00:47:56,311 --> 00:47:57,187
I am.

579
00:47:57,270 --> 00:47:58,814
Still going with that story?

580
00:47:58,897 --> 00:48:00,148
I am your boyfriend.

581
00:48:01,566 --> 00:48:02,776
Is that right?

582
00:48:03,443 --> 00:48:05,529
Did you say we dated for two years?

583
00:48:05,612 --> 00:48:06,446
Yeah.

584
00:48:06,530 --> 00:48:09,032
And we've been living together
since we were in Seoul?

585
00:48:09,700 --> 00:48:12,035
-Yeah.
-Let's say I did pursue you.

586
00:48:12,119 --> 00:48:14,705
You must have liked me back
if you agreed to live with me.

587
00:48:16,373 --> 00:48:17,207
Yeah.

588
00:48:17,791 --> 00:48:19,042
Then you won't mind this.

589
00:48:41,523 --> 00:48:45,944
OUR STICKY LOVE

590
00:49:32,574 --> 00:49:36,536
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

